    "description": "When a user lands on an object tab, Salesforce defaults to the \"Recently Viewed\" list view, whose columns come from the object's Search Layout (\"Search Results\") — NOT from any list view definition. Today those columns are near-empty, so Recently Viewed shows almost no useful data.\n\nUpdate the Search Layouts so Recently Viewed shows the same key fields as the curated Console list views.\n\nObjects (one subtask each):\n\n* Sign_Up__c\n\n* Deal_Rep_Assignment__c\n\n* Deal__c\n\n* Account (Player / Referrer / Operator / Partner record types)\n\n* Study_Link_Click__c\n\nBuild notes:\n\n* Align each column set with the standard column set already agreed in BUILD-17 / BUILD-48 rather than inventing a second convention.\n\n* Search Layouts can be profile-specific — set the Rep-facing set separately from Ops/Admin where the field sets differ (see BUILD-42 rep-facing field cleanup, BUILD-88 no rep access to SLC).\n\n* Do NOT expose Partner on any rep-facing layout (BUILD-21) or Payout/margin-adjacent fields beyond what BUILD-42 allows.\n\n* Also review \"Search Filter Fields\" and the list-view/lookup dialog layouts on the same screen while in there.\n\nRelated: this is the closest we can get to \"defaulting a list view for reps\" — Salesforce cannot set a default list view per profile. See BUILD-115 for the Home Page approach to the same problem.\n\nEffort: \\~4-6h across the 5 objects incl. rep-profile verification.\n\nSource: Kobi, 2026-08-05.",
    "timetracking": {},
    "attachment": [],
    "summary": "BUILD-112 — Search Layouts: key fields on Recently Viewed for all Console objects",
